% layout 'default';
% title 'Something went wrong';

%# Mojolicious renders exception.<mode>.html.ep in preference to
%# exception.html.ep, and exception.html.ep prints the exception inside a
%# <details> block. Without this file that development view was what production
%# served: the message and the source path and line, to whoever triggered it.
%# Reachable unauthenticated -- any die that escapes the workflow dispatcher
%# lands here -- so it leaked internal identifiers and the filesystem layout.
<div class="error-page">
    <h1>Something went wrong</h1>
    <p>We hit an unexpected problem handling that request. Nothing you were
    part-way through has been charged or changed without being recorded.</p>

    %# A page with nothing to quote makes the person describe the problem
    %# instead of naming it. This is the same id the structured log line for
    %# this request carries, so it goes straight to what happened.
    <p class="error-reference">If you need to get in touch about this, quote
    reference <code><%= $c->req->request_id %></code>.</p>

    <a href="/" class="button">Return to Homepage</a>
</div>
